MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The domain moved off Squarespace this morning, so every old URL that is
not mapped is now a live 404 on a domain whose URLs have been indexed for
years.

Redirects: built from the live Squarespace sitemap — 53 URLs, 52 entries.
The 13 blog posts, 4 portfolio pages, the lead magnets, the /store tree,
/home, /links and about ten orphan service pages were all unmapped and
all 404ing. Verified end to end: every source 308s and every destination
returns 200.

Detail-page targets are resolved at build time against the MDX on disk,
using the same draft rule as src/lib/mdx.ts. Every case study and article
is currently published: false, so those 19 redirects send to /work and
/insights rather than passing an old URL's ranking into a 404. Each one
starts pointing at its real page on the build after published: true is
set — nothing to remember later. The build logs which are falling back.

/api/subscribe returned its own configuration error to the browser, and
the form renders that text verbatim: a visitor submitting the audit form
was shown "MailerLite is not configured yet. Set MAILERLITE_API_KEY." It
now logs the reason server-side and gives the visitor the email address
and phone number, so an enquiry is redirected rather than lost while the
MailerLite keys are outstanding. 501 -> 503, which is the accurate code
for a dependency that is not available yet.

Footer: ten anchors on every page pointed at "#" — the four social
profiles, the client portal and five resource links — and the footer
published an internal note to visitors, "Lead-magnet links pending a
migrate/refresh/sunset decision." Social URLs taken from the live
Squarespace site; Client Portal points at portal.ilovedigital.com.au. The
lead-magnet links are removed rather than left dead, since the pages
behind them die with the Squarespace subscription and the
migrate-or-sunset call has not been made. Put them back when the offers
are rebuilt.

Verified: build clean, 17 routes, all 52 redirects resolve to a 200,
form endpoint returns the fallback message, no "#" anchors remain.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
